README for bytescanner

bytescanner is a multi-arch byte scanner and pattern maker for pe elf and raw
files on disk it grows unique ida or x64dbg signatures from offsets you already
know and can try to find those same spots on a later build of the same binary
that later step is a best effort hunt not a guarantee

it reads the files you pass it it does not attach to processes

The commands are as follows:

	gen			-- make unique byte signatures from the offsets you already know
	find			-- look those signatures up in a newer binary and write the new offsets

Run it like this:

	bytescanner gen --bin old.so --csv names.csv --out sigs.csv
	bytescanner find --bin new.so --csv sigs.csv --out names_new.csv
	bytescanner --bin old.so --new new.so --csv names.csv --out names_new.csv

The flags are as follows:

	--bin, -b PATH		-- this is the file you scan on gen it is the old binary and on find it is the new one
	--new PATH		-- path to a newer binary so gen can make signatures then find them in that file in one go
	--old PATH		-- path to the old binary on find so fingerprints have something to compare against
	--csv, -c PATH		-- csv of names and addresses and maybe signatures you already have
	--offsets, -s LIST	-- comma list of hex offsets when you do not have a csv
	--out, -o PATH		-- write the name and address csv here or print it to stdout if you skip this
	--json PATH		-- write extra details to this json file or next to the csv with a json ending
	--format FMT		-- how the signature text looks pick ida or x64dbg
	--arch ARCH		-- force the cpu kind or leave auto so the file header picks it
	--min-len N		-- do not let a signature be shorter than this many bytes
	--max-len N		-- stop growing a signature after this many bytes
	--scope exec|all	-- search only code sections or the whole mapped file
	--all			-- if more than one place matches keep the first hit anyway
	--resolve-conflicts	-- when hits clash compare instruction shape to the old binary and pick one
	--fuzz			-- extra guessy hunt that chops the signature shorter and ranks by fingerprint overlap off unless you pass it
	--mem SIZE		-- how much ram the scan index may use default is 1G you can pass 512M or 50 percent
	--color WHEN		-- color on a tty with auto or force it with always or turn it off with never
	--quiet			-- do not print progress on stderr
	--help, -h		-- print this help

